Product Vision 
Problem: Most clinics in Universities still use manual appointment booking systems where every time students must visit the clinic to be able to schedule appointments. This leads to long waiting times and overcrowding for students as for the clinic staff it will cause inefficient schedule management. Moreover, students may also struggle to know which time slot is available before coming to the clinic.

Target Users: 
University students who need to book medical appointments at their campus clinic.
Clinic staff to be able to manage appointments and monitor their daily schedule.
System administrators to be able to manage user access.

Proposed Solution:
To create a digital clinic appointment booking system that allows students to be able to view available appointment slots beforehand and book clinic visits online. In addition regarding clinic staff it will let them view and manage scheduled appointments efficiently. 

Value of the System:
This system will improve access to healthcare services as students will be able to easily schedule appointments without having to physically visit the clinic beforehand each time. This will reduce the waiting time andalso improve how appointments are organized hence helping the clinic staff to manage everything more effectively. 

Contribution to Sustainable Development Goal 
This project directly supports SDG 3 Good Health and Well-Being by improving access to healthcare services within the university . By changing the whole appointments process into a digital system it will ensure that students can receive medical care more conveniently and efficiently.

